# Party banter at Van Richten's Tower on Lake Baratok. Each node opens with an `if` gate.

~ banter_the_rumor
if flag.tower_rumor and not flag.tower_door_opened
interject tag:curious: A tower in a lake with a lamp in the window and a Vistani with a crossbow on the doorstep. That's either a love story or a siege.
interject tag:blunt: Both. It's usually both.
endif
-> END

~ banter_khazan
if flag.khazan_known and not flag.tower_door_opened
interject class:wizard: A door that opens to a dead man's name. Elegant. Old-fashioned. It assumes nobody would ever be rude enough to say it.
interject class:rogue: I'd have said it on the first day. I say everything on the first day.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ward_for_one
if flag.tower_ward_known and flag.ezmerelda_met_at_tower
interject class:wizard: A ward keyed to one person. You'd have to know her very well. Her voice, her stride, her temper. Months of work, out of love.
interject tag:blunt: Locking someone out isn't love.
interject class:wizard: No. It's what fear does when it's been in love too long.
endif
-> END

~ banter_rictavio
if flag.van_richten_identity_known and not flag.rictavio_unmasked
interject name:silvain_aster: Rictavio. The man in the feathers. That was Rudolph van Richten, and I watched him juggle. I may never recover.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: He juggled badly, if that helps.
interject name:silvain_aster: It does not.
endif
-> END

~ banter_reunited
if flag.van_richten_reunited
interject tag:cheerful: They were shouting at each other for an hour. I think that's the happiest I've seen anyone in this valley.
interject tag:veteran: Old soldiers and their sergeants. You don't shout at people you've stopped caring about.
endif
-> END
